   - **Frequency & Duty**: With TIM1 clocked at 170 MHz, setting $\text{PSC} = 0$ and $\text{ARR} = 8499$ divides the clock by $8500$, generating an exact 20.0 kHz period. Setting $\text{CCR1} = 2125$ achieves an exact $25.0\%$ duty cycle ($2125 / 8500$).
